<speak>It is progressing, although not in a particularly straight line. I no longer attend every warehouse meeting, which has been a useful change. The difficult part is that people still copy me into correspondence simply because they always have. If I reply, the discussion comes back to me. If I stay quiet, someone occasionally assumes that I have not seen something important. I am trying to remain available without becoming the person who settles every small disagreement. That distinction sounds straightforward until a familiar supplier calls me directly and starts asking what I think.</speak>